[TEXT] All evidence is in. Both BGP peers show identical resets ~3-4 minutes ago with **"No path to specified Neighbor (n/a)"** — the FRR reset reason when the interface hosting the peer goes DOWN. The routing table on leaf_router_0_1 confirms: only the local subnet `10.0.1.0/24` via eth2 exists; no BGP routes were learned, so any cross-fabric destination triggers "Destination Net Unreachable" from the gateway.

The spine interfaces (spine_router_0_0:eth2 = UP/LOWER_UP, spine_router_0_1:eth2 = UP/LOWER_UP) are healthy; the fault is exclusively on leaf_router_0_1's side — both eth0 and eth1 are `state DOWN` with no `UP` or `LOWER_UP` kernel flags, indicating they were brought down administratively.

